1
00:00:01,959 --> 00:00:08,799
Chapter 8 Air the half hour ended, five o'clock struck, school was dismissed,

2
00:00:09,620 --> 00:00:11,899
and all were gone into the refractory to tea.

3
00:00:13,110 --> 00:00:14,479
I now ventured to descend.

4
00:00:15,360 --> 00:00:16,540
It was deep dusk.

5
00:00:17,309 --> 00:00:21,221
I retired into a corner and sat down on the floor, the spell

6
00:00:21,222 --> 00:00:25,020
by which I had been so far supported began to dissolve.

7
00:00:25,860 --> 00:00:30,899
Reaction took place, and soon so overwhelming was the grief that seized me.

8
00:00:31,219 --> 00:00:34,059
I sank, prostrate with my face to the ground.

9
00:00:35,120 --> 00:00:36,120
Now I wept.

10
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:38,399
Helen Burns was not here.

11
00:00:39,059 --> 00:00:40,180
Nothing sustained me.

12
00:00:40,790 --> 00:00:44,879
Left to myself, I abandoned myself, and my tears watered the boards.

13
00:00:46,219 --> 00:00:52,540
I had meant to be so good, and to do so much at lowwood, to make so many friends,

14
00:00:52,819 --> 00:00:57,579
to earn respect and win affection, already I had made visible progress.

15
00:00:58,670 --> 00:01:01,879
That very morning I had reached the head of my class.

16
00:01:02,899 --> 00:01:04,780
Miss Miller had praised me warmly.

17
00:01:05,540 --> 00:01:08,000
Miss Temple had smiled at probation.

18
00:01:08,739 --> 00:01:13,680
She had promised to teach me drawing, and to let me learn French, if I continued

19
00:01:13,681 --> 00:01:16,479
to make similar improvement two months longer.

20
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:20,129
And then I was well received by my fellow pupils, treated

21
00:01:20,129 --> 00:01:24,299
as an equal by those of my own age, and not molested by any.

22
00:01:24,979 --> 00:01:29,979
Now, here I lay again, crushed and trodden on, and could I ever rise more?

23
00:01:31,079 --> 00:01:34,500
Never, I thought, and ardently I wished to die.

24
00:01:36,340 --> 00:01:41,840
While sobbing out this wish in broken accents, someone approached, I started up.

25
00:01:42,579 --> 00:01:44,520
Again, Helen Burns was near me.

26
00:01:45,379 --> 00:01:48,840
The fading fires just showed her coming up the long vacant room.

27
00:01:49,620 --> 00:01:50,899
She brought my coffee and bread.

28
00:01:52,719 --> 00:01:55,420
Come, eat something, she said.

29
00:01:56,079 --> 00:01:59,019
But I put both away from me, feeling as if a drop or

30
00:01:59,020 --> 00:02:01,700
a crumb would have choked me in my present condition.

31
00:02:02,760 --> 00:02:05,139
Helen regarded me, probably with surprise.

32
00:02:06,459 --> 00:02:10,459
I could not now abate my agitation though I tried hard.

33
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:13,040
I continued to weep aloud.

34
00:02:14,165 --> 00:02:17,879
She sat down on the ground near me, embraced her knees with her arms,

35
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:20,139
and rested her head upon them.

36
00:02:20,940 --> 00:02:24,120
In that attitude, she remained silent as an Indian.

37
00:02:25,024 --> 00:02:26,239
I was the first who spoke.

38
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:32,760
Helen, why do you stay with a girl whom everybody believes to be a liar?

39
00:02:34,219 --> 00:02:35,340
Everybody, Jane.

40
00:02:36,739 --> 00:02:39,628
Why, there are only 80 people who have heard you

41
00:02:39,629 --> 00:02:42,420
called so, and the world contains hundreds of millions.

42
00:02:43,780 --> 00:02:45,379
But what have I to do with millions?

43
00:02:46,379 --> 00:02:48,319
The 80 I know despise me.

44
00:02:49,680 --> 00:02:50,920
Jane, you are mistaken.

45
00:02:51,700 --> 00:02:54,860
Probably not one in the school either despises or dislikes you.

46
00:02:55,280 --> 00:02:57,299
Many, I am sure, pity you much.

47
00:02:58,510 --> 00:03:02,379
How can they pity me after what Mr. Brockelhurst has said?

48
00:03:03,459 --> 00:03:09,200
Mr. Brockelhurst is not a god, nor is he even a great and admired man.

49
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:11,280
He is little liked here.

50
00:03:12,040 --> 00:03:14,440
He never took steps to make himself liked.

51
00:03:15,520 --> 00:03:20,000
Had he treated you as an a special favourite, you would have found enemies,

52
00:03:20,459 --> 00:03:23,379
declared or covered all around you.

53
00:03:24,569 --> 00:03:29,120
As it is, the greater number would offer you sympathy if they dared.

54
00:03:30,479 --> 00:03:34,331
Teachers and pupils may look coldly on you for a day or

55
00:03:34,332 --> 00:03:37,780
two, but friendly feelings are concealed in their hearts.

56
00:03:38,659 --> 00:03:43,399
And if you persevere in doing well, these feelings will air long appear so

57
00:03:43,400 --> 00:03:47,979
much the more evidently for their temporary suppression, besides Jane.

58
00:03:48,799 --> 00:03:49,799
She paused.

59
00:03:50,469 --> 00:03:54,791
Well, Helen, said I, putting my hand into hers, she

60
00:03:54,792 --> 00:03:59,360
chafed my fingers gently to warm them and went on.

61
00:04:00,760 --> 00:04:05,959
If all the world hated you and believed you wicked, while your own conscience

62
00:04:05,960 --> 00:04:11,440
approved you and absolved you from guilt, you would not be without friends.

63
00:04:12,649 --> 00:04:17,520
No, I know I should think well of myself, but that is not enough.

64
00:04:18,219 --> 00:04:20,979
If others don't love me, I would rather die than live.

65
00:04:21,639 --> 00:04:23,959
I cannot bear to be solitary and hated, Helen.

66
00:04:26,200 --> 00:04:27,200
Look here.

67
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:33,940
To gain some real affection from you, or mistemple, or any other whom I truly

68
00:04:33,941 --> 00:04:40,440
love, I would willingly submit to have the bone of my arm broken, or to let a bull

69
00:04:40,441 --> 00:04:46,441
toss me or to stand behind a kicking horse, and let it dash its hoof at my chest.

70
00:04:47,040 --> 00:04:48,040
Hush, Jane.

71
00:04:48,719 --> 00:04:51,159
You think too much of the love of human beings.

72
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:54,139
You are too impulsive, too vehement.

73
00:04:55,250 --> 00:05:00,700
The sovereign hand that created your frame and put life into it has provided you with

74
00:05:00,700 --> 00:05:05,379
other resources than your feeble self, or than creatures feeble as you.

75
00:05:06,864 --> 00:05:10,762
Besides this earth and besides the race of men,

76
00:05:10,763 --> 00:05:14,360
there is an invisible world and a kingdom of spirits.

77
00:05:15,190 --> 00:05:20,920
That world is round us, for it is everywhere, and those spirits watch us,

78
00:05:21,420 --> 00:05:23,500
for they are commissioned to guard us.

79
00:05:24,170 --> 00:05:29,280
And if we were dying in pain and shame, if scorned, smote us on all sides,

80
00:05:29,920 --> 00:05:35,360
and hatred crushed us, angels see our tortures, recognize our innocence,

81
00:05:36,059 --> 00:05:41,920
if innocent we be, as I know you are of this charge, which Mr. Brockelhurst has

82
00:05:41,921 --> 00:05:45,739
weakly and pompously repeated at second hand, from Mrs. Reed.

83
00:05:46,500 --> 00:05:51,719
For I read a sincere nature in your ardent eyes and on your clear front, and God

84
00:05:51,720 --> 00:05:57,780
waits only the separation of spirit from flesh to crown us with a full reward.

85
00:05:58,579 --> 00:05:59,579
Why then?

86
00:06:00,520 --> 00:06:02,780
Should we ever sink overwhelmed with distress?

87
00:06:03,760 --> 00:06:08,299
When life is so soon over and death is so certain and entrance to happiness,

88
00:06:09,500 --> 00:06:10,500
to glory?

89
00:06:11,959 --> 00:06:12,959
I was silent.

90
00:06:13,840 --> 00:06:17,229
Helen had calmed me, but in the tranquility she

91
00:06:17,230 --> 00:06:21,319
imparted, there was an alloy of inexpressible sadness.

92
00:06:22,579 --> 00:06:27,239
I felt the impression of woe as she spoke, but I could not tell when it came.

93
00:06:28,260 --> 00:06:34,060
And when, having done speaking, she breathed a little fast and coughed a short cough.

94
00:06:34,500 --> 00:06:39,840
I momentarily forgot my own sorrows, to yield to a vague concern for her.

95
00:06:41,040 --> 00:06:45,079
Resting my head on Helen's shoulder, I put my arms around her waist.

96
00:06:45,799 --> 00:06:49,559
She drew me to her, and we reposed in silence.

97
00:06:51,024 --> 00:06:54,079
We had not sat long thus when another person came in.

98
00:06:54,930 --> 00:07:00,719
Some heavy clouds swept from the sky by a rising wind, had left the moon bare,

99
00:07:01,340 --> 00:07:07,579
and her light, streaming in through a window near, shone full both on us and on

100
00:07:07,581 --> 00:07:11,659
the approaching figure, which we at once recognized as Miss Temple.

101
00:07:13,354 --> 00:07:16,780
I came on purpose to find you, Jane Eyre, said she.

102
00:07:17,440 --> 00:07:22,360
I want you in my room, and as Helen burns is with you, she may come too.

103
00:07:24,239 --> 00:07:25,239
We went.

104
00:07:25,889 --> 00:07:30,780
Following the superintendent's guidance, we had to thread some intricate passages,

105
00:07:31,459 --> 00:07:34,219
and mount a staircase before we reached her apartment.

106
00:07:35,219 --> 00:07:38,200
It contained a good fire, and looked cheerful.

107
00:07:44,280 --> 00:07:52,280
Miss Temple told Helen burns to be seated in a low armchair on one side of the

108
00:07:52,281 --> 00:07:56,459
looking down at my face, have you cried your grief away?

109
00:07:58,059 --> 00:07:59,920
I am afraid I never shall do that.

110
00:08:00,639 --> 00:08:01,639
Why?

111
00:08:02,375 --> 00:08:05,290
Because I have been wrongly accused, and you,

112
00:08:05,290 --> 00:08:08,159
ma'am, and everybody else will now think me wicked.

113
00:08:09,340 --> 00:08:13,300
We shall think you, what you prove yourself to be my child,

114
00:08:13,301 --> 00:08:17,379
continue to act as a good girl, and you will satisfy us.

115
00:08:18,520 --> 00:08:19,520
Shall I, Miss Temple?

116
00:08:20,809 --> 00:08:24,020
You will, said she, passing her arm around me.

117
00:08:24,959 --> 00:08:29,680
And now tell me who is the lady whom Mr. Brocklehurst called your benefactress.

118
00:08:31,549 --> 00:08:36,620
Mrs. Reed, my uncle's wife, my uncle is dead, and he left me to her care.

119
00:08:37,989 --> 00:08:40,360
Did she not then adopt you of her own accord?

120
00:08:41,620 --> 00:08:44,559
No, ma'am, she was sorry to have to do it.

121
00:08:45,100 --> 00:08:48,858
But my uncle, as I have often heard the servants say, got

122
00:08:48,859 --> 00:08:52,440
her to promise before he died that she would always keep me.

123
00:08:54,079 --> 00:08:59,459
Well, now, Jane, you know, or at least I will tell you that when a criminal is

124
00:08:59,460 --> 00:09:02,899
accused, he is always allowed to speak in his own defence.

125
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:05,600
You have been charged with falsehood.

126
00:09:06,180 --> 00:09:08,100
Defend yourself to me as well as you can.

127
00:09:08,719 --> 00:09:13,360
Say whatever your memory suggests is true, but add nothing and exaggerate nothing.

128
00:09:14,620 --> 00:09:21,040
I resolved in the depth of my heart that I would be most moderate, most correct,

129
00:09:21,969 --> 00:09:27,021
and having reflected a few minutes in order to arrange coherently what I had to say.

130
00:09:27,450 --> 00:09:32,840
I told her all the story of my sad childhood, exhausted by emotion.

131
00:09:33,659 --> 00:09:39,140
My language was more subdued than it generally was when it developed that sad theme.

132
00:09:39,610 --> 00:09:45,340
And mindful of Helen's warnings against the indulgence of resentment, I infused

133
00:09:45,341 --> 00:09:49,739
into the narrative far less of goal and wormwood than ordinary.

134
00:09:50,659 --> 00:09:53,639
Thus restrained and simplified, it sounded more credible.

135
00:09:55,069 --> 00:09:59,559
I felt as I went on, that Miss Temple fully believed me.

136
00:10:00,760 --> 00:10:03,114
In the course of the tale, I had mentioned

137
00:10:03,115 --> 00:10:06,761
Mr. Lloyd as having come to see me after the fit.

138
00:10:07,569 --> 00:10:12,479
For I never forgot the, to me, frightful episode of the red room,

139
00:10:13,420 --> 00:10:18,840
in detailing which my excitement was sure, in some degree, to break bounds.

140
00:10:19,920 --> 00:10:24,540
For nothing could soften in my recollection the spasm of agony which

141
00:10:24,540 --> 00:10:30,020
clutched my heart when Mrs. Reed spurned my wild supplication for pardon and locked

142
00:10:30,021 --> 00:10:32,739
me a second time in the dark and haunted chamber.

143
00:10:33,940 --> 00:10:35,200
I had finished.

144
00:10:36,059 --> 00:10:38,440
Miss Temple regarded me a few minutes in silence.

145
00:10:39,280 --> 00:10:43,420
She then said, I know something of Mr. Lloyd.

146
00:10:44,139 --> 00:10:45,139
I shall write to him.

147
00:10:45,680 --> 00:10:48,343
If his reply agrees with your statement, you

148
00:10:48,343 --> 00:10:51,720
shall be publicly cleared from every imputation.

149
00:10:52,260 --> 00:10:55,159
To me, Jane, you are clear now.

150
00:10:56,540 --> 00:11:02,459
She kissed me, and still keeping me at her side, where I was well-contented to stand.

151
00:11:03,149 --> 00:11:07,600
For I derived a child's pleasure from the contemplation of her face, her dress,

152
00:11:08,180 --> 00:11:12,819
her one or two ornaments, her white forehead, her clustered and shining curls,

153
00:11:13,459 --> 00:11:15,059
and beaming dark eyes.

154
00:11:16,040 --> 00:11:17,920
She proceeded to address Helen Burns.

155
00:11:19,270 --> 00:11:20,540
How are you tonight, Helen?

156
00:11:21,079 --> 00:11:22,200
Have you coughed much today?

157
00:11:23,739 --> 00:11:25,459
Not quite so much, I think, ma'am.

158
00:11:26,389 --> 00:11:27,520
And the pain in your chest?

159
00:11:28,780 --> 00:11:29,780
It is a little better.

160
00:11:30,680 --> 00:11:34,399
Miss Temple got up, took her hand and examined her pulse.

161
00:11:35,270 --> 00:11:37,159
Then she returned to her own seat.

162
00:11:38,100 --> 00:11:40,879
As she resumed it, I heard her sigh low.

163
00:11:41,799 --> 00:11:43,020
She was pensive a few minutes.

164
00:11:43,770 --> 00:11:45,959
Then rousing herself, she said cheerfully.

165
00:11:47,645 --> 00:11:49,479
But you two are my visitors tonight.

166
00:11:50,020 --> 00:11:51,440
I must treat you as such.

167
00:11:52,079 --> 00:11:53,079
She rang her bell.

168
00:11:54,340 --> 00:11:57,559
Barbara, she said to the servant who answered it.

169
00:11:58,540 --> 00:11:59,760
I have not yet had tea.

170
00:12:00,680 --> 00:12:03,440
Bring the tray and place cups for these two young ladies.

171
00:12:04,729 --> 00:12:06,260
And a tray was soon brought.

172
00:12:07,340 --> 00:12:10,941
How pretty, to my eyes, did the china cups and bright

173
00:12:10,941 --> 00:12:14,000
teapot look placed on the little round table near the fire.

174
00:12:14,760 --> 00:12:19,139
How fragrant was the steam of the beverage and the scent of the toast.

175
00:12:20,020 --> 00:12:24,979
Of which, however, I, to my dismay, for I was beginning to be hungry.

176
00:12:25,860 --> 00:12:28,579
Dissearned only a very small portion.

177
00:12:29,760 --> 00:12:31,360
Miss Temple dissearned it, too.

178
00:12:32,979 --> 00:12:37,440
Barbara said she, can you not bring a little more bread and butter?

179
00:12:38,379 --> 00:12:40,000
There is not enough for three.

180
00:12:41,579 --> 00:12:42,819
Barbara went out.

181
00:12:43,399 --> 00:12:44,700
She returned soon.

182
00:12:45,840 --> 00:12:49,700
Madam, Mrs. Hardin says she has sent up the usual quantity.

183
00:12:50,579 --> 00:12:53,739
Mrs. Hardin, be it observed, was the housekeeper.

184
00:12:54,420 --> 00:12:57,092
A woman after Mr. Brocklehurst's own heart,

185
00:12:57,093 --> 00:13:00,540
made up of equal parts of whalebone and iron.

186
00:13:01,370 --> 00:13:03,799
Oh, very well, returned Miss Temple.

187
00:13:04,399 --> 00:13:06,159
We must make it do, Barbara, I suppose.

188
00:13:07,219 --> 00:13:09,700
And as the girl withdrew, she added smiling.

189
00:13:10,549 --> 00:13:15,280
Fortunately, I have it in my power to supply deficiencies for this once.

190
00:13:17,600 --> 00:13:22,579
Having invited Helen and me to approach the table, and placed before each of us a

191
00:13:22,581 --> 00:13:29,399
cup of tea with one delicious but thin morsel of toast, she got up, unlocked a

192
00:13:29,400 --> 00:13:32,984
drawer, and taking from it a whistle wrapped in paper

193
00:13:32,985 --> 00:13:37,420
disclosed presently to our eyes a good-sized seed cake.

194
00:13:38,989 --> 00:13:44,840
I meant to give each of you some of this to take with you, said she, but as there

195
00:13:44,841 --> 00:13:48,047
is so little toast, you must have it now, and

196
00:13:48,048 --> 00:13:51,460
she proceeded to cut slices with a generous hand.

197
00:13:52,430 --> 00:13:55,659
We feasted that evening as on nectar and embrosia.

198
00:13:56,920 --> 00:14:01,079
And not the least delight of the entertainment was the smile of

199
00:14:01,081 --> 00:14:06,040
gratification with which our hostess regarded us, as we satisfied our famished

200
00:14:06,040 --> 00:14:08,760
appetites on the delicate fare she liberally supplied.

201
00:14:09,629 --> 00:14:13,840
Tea over and the tray removed, she again summoned us to the fire.

202
00:14:14,780 --> 00:14:18,979
We sat one on each side of her, and now a conversation followed between

203
00:14:18,980 --> 00:14:23,440
her and Helen, which it was indeed a privilege to be admitted to here.

204
00:14:24,549 --> 00:14:29,959
Miss Temple had always something of serenity in her air, of state in her mean,

205
00:14:31,040 --> 00:14:36,899
of refined propriety in her language, which precluded deviation into the ardent,

206
00:14:37,379 --> 00:14:44,260
the excited, the eager, something which chastened the pleasure of those who looked

207
00:14:48,020 --> 00:14:56,020
on her and listened to her by a Helen Burns, I was struck with wonder.

208
00:14:56,840 --> 00:15:02,459
The refreshing meal, the brilliant fire, the presence and kindness of her beloved

209
00:15:02,460 --> 00:15:08,600
instructoress, or perhaps more than all these, something in her own unique mind

210
00:15:08,899 --> 00:15:10,860
had roused her powers within her.

211
00:15:11,840 --> 00:15:13,540
They woke, they kindled.

212
00:15:14,739 --> 00:15:18,846
First, they glowed in the bright tint of her cheek, which

213
00:15:18,847 --> 00:15:22,520
till this hour I had never seen but pale and bloodless.

214
00:15:23,700 --> 00:15:28,079
Then they shone in the liquid luster of her eyes, which had suddenly acquired a

215
00:15:28,081 --> 00:15:31,399
beauty, more singular than that of Miss Temple's.

216
00:15:32,260 --> 00:15:37,000
A beauty neither of fine colour, nor long eyelash, nor penciled brow,

217
00:15:37,620 --> 00:15:41,239
but of meaning, of movement, of radiance.

218
00:15:42,469 --> 00:15:48,240
Then her soul sat on her lips, and language flowed from what source I cannot tell.

219
00:15:49,139 --> 00:15:53,145
Has a girl of 14, a heart large enough, vigorous enough,

220
00:15:53,146 --> 00:15:58,040
to hold a swelling spring of pure, full, fervid eloquence?

221
00:15:59,049 --> 00:16:04,980
Such was the characteristic of Helen's discourse on that, to me, memorable evening.

222
00:16:05,479 --> 00:16:09,549
Her spirit seemed hastening to live within a very brief

223
00:16:09,550 --> 00:16:13,040
span, as much as many live during a protracted existence.

224
00:16:14,250 --> 00:16:18,760
They conversed of things I had never heard of, of nations and times past,

225
00:16:19,600 --> 00:16:21,059
of countries far away.

226
00:16:22,100 --> 00:16:25,020
Of secrets of nature discovered or guessed at.

227
00:16:25,690 --> 00:16:31,841
They spoke of books, how many they had read, what stores of knowledge they possessed.

228
00:16:32,350 --> 00:16:35,819
Then they seemed so familiar with French names and French authors.

229
00:16:37,245 --> 00:16:43,020
But my amazement reached its climax, when Miss Temple asked Helen, if she

230
00:16:43,021 --> 00:16:47,079
sometimes snatched a moment to recall the Latin her father had taught her,

231
00:16:47,899 --> 00:16:51,959
and taking a book from a shelf, bade her read and construe a page of

232
00:16:51,960 --> 00:16:58,700
Virgil, and Helen obeyed, my organ of veneration expanding at every sounding line.

233
00:16:59,239 --> 00:17:02,840
She had scarcely finished air the bell announced, bed time.

234
00:17:03,829 --> 00:17:05,120
No delay could be admitted.

235
00:17:06,020 --> 00:17:09,475
Miss Temple embraced us both, saying, as she

236
00:17:09,476 --> 00:17:13,240
drew us to her heart, God bless you my children.

237
00:17:13,579 --> 00:17:16,000
Helen, she held a little longer than me.

238
00:17:16,760 --> 00:17:18,379
She let her go more reluctantly.

239
00:17:19,379 --> 00:17:21,600
It was Helen her eye followed to the door.

240
00:17:22,500 --> 00:17:26,239
It was for her she a second time breathed a sad sigh.

241
00:17:27,200 --> 00:17:29,520
For her she wiped a tear from her cheek.

242
00:17:31,379 --> 00:17:35,200
On reaching the bedroom we heard the voice of Miss Scratchard.

243
00:17:36,149 --> 00:17:37,440
She was examining draws.

244
00:17:38,219 --> 00:17:43,399
She had just pulled out Helen Burns's, and when we entered Helen was greeted with

245
00:17:43,400 --> 00:17:47,735
a sharp reprimand, and told that tomorrow she should have half

246
00:17:47,736 --> 00:17:51,180
a dozen of untidely folded articles pinned to her shoulder.

247
00:17:52,879 --> 00:17:59,681
My things were indeed in shameful disorder, murmured Helen to me in a low voice.

248
00:18:00,319 --> 00:18:03,440
I intended to have arranged them, but I forgot.

249
00:18:05,450 --> 00:18:10,659
Next morning, Miss Scratchard wrote in conspicuous characters on a piece of

250
00:18:10,661 --> 00:18:16,742
pasteboard the word Slatton, and bound it like a factory, round

251
00:18:16,743 --> 00:18:20,700
Helen's large mild intelligent and benign looking forehead.

252
00:18:21,694 --> 00:18:25,664
She wore it till evening, patient, unresentful,

253
00:18:25,665 --> 00:18:28,900
regarding it as a deserved punishment.

254
00:18:29,610 --> 00:18:33,959
The moment Miss Scratchard withdrew after afternoon school, I ran to Helen,

255
00:18:34,540 --> 00:18:38,806
tore it off, and thrust it into the fire, the fury of which

256
00:18:38,807 --> 00:18:42,559
she was incapable had been burning in my soul all day.

257
00:18:43,694 --> 00:18:49,700
And tears, hot and large, had continually been scolding my cheek.

258
00:18:50,680 --> 00:18:56,879
For the spectacle of her sad resignation, gave me an intolerable pain at the heart.

259
00:18:58,569 --> 00:19:03,182
About a week subsequently to the incidents above narrated,

260
00:19:03,183 --> 00:19:08,319
Miss Temple, who had written to Mr Lloyd, received his answer.

261
00:19:09,610 --> 00:19:13,840
It appeared that what he said went to corroborate my account.

262
00:19:15,149 --> 00:19:20,780
Miss Temple, having assembled the school, announced that inquiry had been made into

263
00:19:20,781 --> 00:19:25,819
the charges alleged against Jane Eyre, and that she was most happy to be able to

264
00:19:25,820 --> 00:19:29,219
pronounce her completely cleared from every imputation.

265
00:19:30,370 --> 00:19:34,495
The teachers then shook hands with me and kissed me, and a

266
00:19:34,495 --> 00:19:37,579
murmur of pleasure ran through the ranks of my companions.

267
00:19:38,899 --> 00:19:43,700
Thus relieved of a grievous load, I, from that hour set to work afresh,

268
00:19:44,340 --> 00:19:48,549
resolved to pioneer my way through every difficulty, I

269
00:19:48,549 --> 00:19:52,340
toiled hard, and my success was proportionate to my efforts.

270
00:19:53,239 --> 00:19:59,399
My memory, not naturally tenacious, improved with practice, exercise,

271
00:20:00,120 --> 00:20:04,500
sharpen my wits, in a few weeks I was promoted to a higher class.

272
00:20:05,360 --> 00:20:09,239
In less than two months, I was allowed to commence French and drawing.

273
00:20:10,159 --> 00:20:15,239
I learned the first two tenses of the verb Etre, and sketched my first cottage,

274
00:20:15,680 --> 00:20:20,680
whose walls, by the by, outrivaled in slope those of the leaning tower of Pisa,

275
00:20:21,219 --> 00:20:22,219
on the same day.

276
00:20:23,590 --> 00:20:30,139
That night, on going to bed, I forgot to prepare in imagination the barmicide

277
00:20:30,140 --> 00:20:33,691
supper of hot roast potatoes, or white bread and new

278
00:20:33,692 --> 00:20:37,479
milk, with which I was want to amuse my inward cravings.

279
00:20:38,670 --> 00:20:44,079
I feasted instead on the spectacle of ideal drawings, which I saw in the dark.

280
00:20:45,090 --> 00:20:51,120
All the work of my own hands, freely penciled houses and trees, picturesque

281
00:20:51,120 --> 00:20:56,280
rocks and ruins, kipe-like groups of cattle, sweet paintings of butterflies

282
00:20:56,281 --> 00:21:02,299
hovering over unblown roses, of birds picking at ripe cherries, of wren's nests

283
00:21:02,300 --> 00:21:07,319
and closing pearl-like eggs, wreathed about with young ivy sprays.

284
00:21:08,750 --> 00:21:13,219
I examined, too, in thought, the possibility of my ever being able to

285
00:21:13,220 --> 00:21:19,319
translate currently, a certain little French story, which Madame Pierrot had

286
00:21:19,320 --> 00:21:22,524
that day shown me, nor was that problem solved

287
00:21:22,525 --> 00:21:25,879
in my satisfaction air I fell sweetly asleep.

288
00:21:27,579 --> 00:21:31,771
Well has Solomon said, better is a dinner of herbs

289
00:21:31,772 --> 00:21:36,540
where love is, than a stalled ox and hatred therewith.

290
00:21:37,620 --> 00:21:40,224
I would not now have exchanged lowwood with all its

291
00:21:40,225 --> 00:21:43,040
privations for gateshead and its daily luxuries.

292
00:21:45,674 --> 00:21:46,674
Chapter 9.

293
00:21:48,899 --> 00:21:54,299
But the privations, or rather the hardships of lowwood lessened, spring drew on.

294
00:21:54,809 --> 00:21:56,479
She was indeed already come.

295
00:21:57,120 --> 00:22:01,680
The frosts of winter had ceased, its snows were melted, its cutting winds

296
00:22:01,681 --> 00:22:05,000
ameliorated, my wretched feet flayed and swollen to lameness by the sharp air of
